*------------------------------------------------------ 160 ptw_min_fence_alttop
*  CLASS (a) IN BEAUTY'S OWN SHAPE -- beauty's Real (line 55) and White (line 70) are both an ALT
*  TOP with a FENCE nested inside an arm: ( X FENCE(..) .. | Y ).  Same signature as the witness
*  above (pfenced=1 right_sealed=0 rn=0), but SCRIP_FENCE_IGNORE=1 DOES NOT CURE IT -- publishing
*  the first-allocated body node as the carrier lands INSIDE arm 1, not on the ALT, so the blob
*  still cannot offer arm 2.  The fence-free control ptw_min_alttop_nofence_ctl proves that second
*  wall exists with no fence anywhere.
          P = ( 'a' FENCE(epsilon) | 'aa' )
          'aa' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)                :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*---------------------------------------------- 161 ptw_min_fence_left_altresume
*  CLASS (a) PURE FENCE REFUSAL -- pfenced=1 right_sealed=0 rn=0, the PAT$12/PAT$20 signature.
*  The blob's live resume surface is the TRAILING alternation, but the s182 tier-1 narrowing only
*  publishes a carrier when the FIRST body node is an ARBNO/ARB/BAL generator, so this blob keeps
*  body_root=NULL and concedes wholesale at beta.  SCRIP_FENCE_IGNORE=1 CURES IT: the fence verdict
*  is the whole refusal here.  De-fenced twin ( 'a' | 'aa' ) is green.
          P = FENCE(epsilon) ( 'a' | 'aa' )
          'aa' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)                :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
