*------------------------------------------------------- 171 ptw_min_poison_eval
*  s182 -- THE POISON IS THE ON-RAMP, AND EVAL REACHES IT TOO.
*  One EVAL anywhere sets g_sno_fz_unsafe (lower_snobol4.c:1001), which unseals EVERY
*  name in the program, so `P2 = A B` cannot fold and NO PAT$ blob graph is emitted.
*  The defer then runs the generic C road, which silently loses ARBNO retry.
          Q = EVAL('1')
          A = ARBNO('a')
          B = ''
          P2 = A B
          'aa' POS(0) *P2 RPOS(0)               :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
 $('Z' 'Z') = 1; P1 = LEN(3) | LEN(2) LEN(2); 'abcdef' POS(0) *P1 'ef' RPOS(0) :S(OK)F(NO);OK OUTPUT = 'match' :(END);NO OUTPUT = 'nomatch';END;* ptw_min_refusal
*------------------------------------------------- 173 ptw_min_rseal_arbno XFAIL
*  CLASS (b) RIGHT-SEALED REFUSAL -- right_sealed=1, the PAT$13/PAT$22/PAT$28 signature, a SECOND
*  refusal the s182 fence work does not touch.  sno_pat_right_sealed seals the WHOLE blob because
*  its RIGHTMOST element is a fence form, but the manual's seal only forbids re-offering the FENCE'S
*  OWN alternatives -- the ARBNO to the fence's LEFT still has instances to give, and reaching it
*  never backs up THROUGH the fence.  SCRIP_FENCE_IGNORE=1 does not cure it (right_sealed short-
*  circuits the carrier the fence path computed: rn=1 brt=1 and the ternary discards both).
          P = ARBNO('a') FENCE('b' | epsilon)
          'aab' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)               :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*---------------------------------------------- 174 ptw_min_rseal_commands XFAIL
*  CLASS (b) IN BEAUTY'S OWN SHAPE -- beauty's Commands (line 217) verbatim:
*      Commands = *Command FENCE(*Commands | epsilon)
*  with Command given real alternatives, which is what beauty's Command has.  The left element's
*  alternatives are exactly what the wholesale seal throws away.  beauty's X4 (line 128) is the same
*  shape one element wider.
          Command = 'a' | 'ab'
          Commands = *Command FENCE(*Commands | epsilon)
          'ab' POS(0) *Commands RPOS(0)         :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*------------------------------------------ 175 ptw_min_rseal_unsealed_ctl XFAIL
*  CONTROL THAT SEPARATES THE TWO REFUSALS BY ONE TOKEN.  Identical to ptw_min_rseal_arbno with a
*  trailing epsilon appended, which moves the fence off the right end: right_sealed flips 1 -> 0 and
*  nothing else changes.  Default arm: still red (the fence refusal is now the one firing).
*  SCRIP_FENCE_IGNORE=1: GREEN.  So the seal and the fence verdict are two independent refusals on
*  the same blob, and only the fence half was narrowed at s182.
          P = ARBNO('a') FENCE('b' | epsilon) epsilon
          'aab' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)               :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
